# Ignore ALL wmake-generated build folders
**/linux64Gcc**/

# Ignore object files and dep files (even if outside that folder)
*.o
*.dep

# Ignore OpenFOAM wmake temporary metadata
sourceFiles
variables

# Ignore tests folder
/tests

# Ignore TODO file
/TODO.md

/auxFiles

# Ignore vscode files
.vscode


# SMOKE BEDS: track the case DEFINITIONS, ignore the run output.
#
# These were ignored wholesale as "local validation/scratch run directories",
# and that is exactly why they rotted. Being invisible to `git status` meant no
# key-rename sweep ever reached them, and by 2026-09-02 all five carried FOUR
# settings the solver had come to reject and none of them could start:
# limitVoltageRiseRate + maxVoltageRiseRate, a dangling appliedVoltage, a
# missing electronEnergyModel, and an unsplit chemistrySolver. They are the
# smoke tests -- the thing that is supposed to catch a broken build -- and they
# were themselves broken and unnoticed.
#
# The run output is genuinely scratch, and 614 MB of it, so only that is
# ignored.
#
# NOTE the time-directory patterns deliberately do NOT use `[0-9]*`, which
# matches `0.orig` and would ignore the initial-field TEMPLATES. That glob has
# already destroyed 0.orig twice here; the failure surfaces much later as
# "cannot find file .../0/ePotential", which names the wrong thing entirely.
smoke/*/0/
smoke/*/[0-9]*.[0-9]*/
smoke/*/[0-9]*e-[0-9]*/
smoke/*/logs/
smoke/*/postProcessing/
smoke/*/log.*
smoke/*/run.log
smoke/*/case.foam
smoke/*/constant/polyMesh/
smoke/*/constant/plasmaTables/
# NOT `smoke/*/constant/*/`: that would silently ignore per-region
# material files (constant/<region>/electricalProperties) if a smoke bed
# ever became multi-region -- the same invisibility that caused this mess.
smoke/*/system/*/
# build artefacts: generated from fvSolution-foam / etc/changeDictionary
smoke/*/system/fvSolution
smoke/*/system/changeDictionaryDict

# per-component build logs and local run helpers: machine-specific, and they
# churn on every build
buildlogs/
build.log
rebuild.log

# local run helpers: personal workflow, not part of the toolkit. build-all.sh
# is kept -- it is the documented, dependency-ordered build entry point.
watchdog.sh
check-run.sh
make-smoke-case.sh
rerun.sh
run-guarded.sh
run-long.sh

# GENERATED SOLUTION DICTIONARIES in our own tutorials.
#
# Allrun does `cp system/fvSolution-foam system/fvSolution` (or -petsc,
# selected by `matrixSolver`) and `cp etc/changeDictionary.<region>
# system/changeDictionaryDict`. Both destinations are BUILD ARTEFACTS: an edit
# to them is silently overwritten on the next run, and they were tracked in
# some cases and not others though every case generates them.
#
# EDIT system/fvSolution-foam AND etc/changeDictionary.* INSTEAD.
tutorials/**/system/fvSolution
tutorials/**/system/changeDictionaryDict

# EXCEPT needleDBD, whose system/fvSolution is HAND-AUTHORED and is the only
# copy: that case has no -foam/-petsc pair, because the pair exists solely to
# switch linear-solver backends and an OpenFOAM solver dictionary silently
# ignores entries it does not use -- so one `ePotential` block carries both
# and `$ePotentialSolver` picks one. A `-foam` suffix with no `-petsc` sibling
# buys nothing and costs the artefact trap above.
!tutorials/plasma/soPlasmaFoam/needleDBD/system/fvSolution

# ThirdParty/ is deliberately untouched: those fvSolution files are upstream
# case definitions, not generated by anything here.

# The extruded mesh is reproducible in <1 s from the 2-D one by
# tools/msh2Dto3D.py (see SoEEDF meshes/README.md). 14 MB is not worth tracking.
tutorials/**/*_extruded.msh

# Per-region STUBS written by tools/plasmaSetupRegions.sh. Ten-line files whose
# only content is `#include "../<same name>"`, regenerated after every split
# (splitMeshRegions overwrites them with empty dummies). Nothing to track.
tutorials/**/constant/*/plasmaSpeciesProperties
tutorials/**/constant/*/plasmaTransportProperties
tutorials/**/constant/*/photoionizationProperties

# Per-region system/ directories: fvSchemes and fvSolution stubs, same as above.
tutorials/**/system/*/

# ------------------------------------------------------------ validation/ ----
#
# EXACTLY THE smoke/ PRINCIPLE ABOVE: track the case DEFINITION, ignore what a
# RUN produces. Extended here 2026-09-11 because validation/ had been tracked
# WHOLESALE -- 3228 files, of which ~2600 were output -- and that made rule D4
# ("tell me about uncommitted work; NEW UNTRACKED FILES ARE THE URGENT CASE")
# structurally unable to fire: `git status` stood at 1310 lines, 1302 of them
# here, and buried in them were two genuinely new source files (ROUNDW.C/.H)
# and a real portability fix. A status nobody can read is a status nobody
# reads.
#
# The measured split: logs/ alone was 1.1 GB of TRACKED text. plasmaTables 36 MB
# (regenerated by each case's own Allrun-serial, `--EN 1:55000:261`), polyMesh
# 9.6 MB (blockMesh/gmshToFoam), the .msh 14 MB (gmsh, from the .geo that IS
# tracked).
#
# KEPT, because they are the case DEFINITION and nothing regenerates them:
#   configuration/{config,boundaries}   COMPARE.md   Allrun-serial   run.sh
#   system/* (except the two generated below)        etc/changeDictionary.*
#   constant/* (mechanism .foam/.mech.json, properties)   0.orig/
#   *.geo (the mesh SOURCE)   the analysis *.py   the top-level *.md
#
# NOTE the time-directory globs deliberately do NOT use `[0-9]*`, for the same
# reason recorded in the smoke section: it matches `0.orig` and would ignore
# the initial-field TEMPLATES. There are 24 `0.orig/` under validation/. The
# patterns below require a DIGIT after the dot, so `0.orig` cannot match --
# verified with `git check-ignore` before this stanza was committed.
validation/**/logs/
validation/**/postProcessing/
validation/**/processor[0-9]*/
validation/**/VTK/
validation/**/constant/polyMesh/
validation/**/constant/plasmaTables/
validation/**/0/
validation/**/[0-9]*.[0-9]*/
validation/**/[0-9]*e-[0-9]*/
validation/**/log.*
validation/**/run.log
validation/**/case.foam
# Field SNAPSHOTS kept beside a case for restart/comparison (rule B1's use
# side). Same content as a time directory, different name: 142 MB in one sweep.
validation/**/.snapshot*/
validation/**/gdb_newton/
# ionTables sit next to plasmaTables and are generated the same way.
validation/**/ionTables/
# Solver logs written at the validation/ ROOT rather than inside a case --
# `validation/pcfix_maxit_dt1e-9.log` alone is 33 MB. `log.*` above does not
# match these because the name is <arm>.log, not log.<utility>.
validation/*.log
validation/**/*.log
# Bulk analysis dumps at a case root (runaway.csv was 26 MB). Deliberately
# `*/*.csv`, one level only: validation/<case>/profiles/*.csv is a kept,
# hand-curated extraction and sits one level deeper.
validation/*/*.csv
# NOT `validation/**/*.foam`: `constant/argon_plasma.foam` is the MECHANISM,
# a tracked input, and a blanket glob would silently drop it.
validation/**/*.msh
validation/**/system/fvSolution
validation/**/system/changeDictionaryDict

# ---------------------------------------------------------- verification/ ----
#
# The OPPOSITE problem: verification/ -- the analytic-ground-truth suite, the
# only place in the tree with an exact solution to check against -- was
# UNTRACKED IN ITS ENTIRETY, so a `git clean` would have destroyed it and no
# documentation sweep could ever reach it. That is precisely how the smoke beds
# rotted. It is 6.8 MB; the beds, reports, baselines and figures are now tracked
# and only the run output is ignored.
verification/**/logs/
verification/**/processor[0-9]*/
verification/**/sweep.out

# ------------------------------------------------------------- tutorials/ ----
# The tutorials carry the same generated artefacts as the validation cases; the
# stanza above already covers their dictionaries, this covers their run output.
tutorials/**/constant/polyMesh/
tutorials/**/constant/ionTables/
#
# NOT `tutorials/**/constant/plasmaTables/`, though smoke/ and validation/ both
# ignore exactly that path. THE TUTORIALS MUST SHIP THEIR TABLES, because --
# unlike every validation case, whose Allrun-serial regenerates them with
# `--EN 1:55000:261 -o constant/plasmaTables` -- the tutorial Allrun-serial
# does NOT (checked 2026-09-11: 0 of 1 Allrun files mention them). Ignoring
# them would leave a fresh clone unable to start
# positiveStreamer_LMEA_fast, which is THE coarse debugging bed at ~2 s/run and
# the thing every Newton defect of 2026-09-11 was actually found on.
# The mesh is a different matter and IS ignored above: those cases carry a
# system/blockMeshDict and their Allrun does blockMesh + refineMesh.
tutorials/**/postProcessing/
tutorials/**/processor[0-9]*/
tutorials/**/logs/
tutorials/**/log.*
tutorials/**/case.foam

# Locally built PETSc (1.3 GB, ThirdParty/petsc-3.24.0). Built from source per
# docs/getting_started/petsc4foam.md; PETSC_DIR is set by etc/bashrc.
ThirdParty/petsc-3.24.0/

# Claude Code session-local state: the hook event log and the kill switch.
# The skills, agents, settings.json and hooks themselves ARE tracked.
.claude/hook-events.log
.claude/hooks-off
.claude/settings.local.json
